---
id: PAT-001
name: Idiomatic Rust Patterns for Security-Critical Code
---

# Rust Patterns Catalog

## RAII Security Guards
Pattern: Implement `Drop` to auto-restore/zero security-critical state.

### Examples
| Guard | File | Purpose |
|-------|------|---------|
| `SpoofGuard` | stack_spoof.rs | Restores original return address on drop |
| `StompGuard` | func_stomp.rs | Restores original function bytes on drop |
| `SecureVec` | crypto.rs | Zeroes memory on drop |
| `NtVecBuf` | winhttp_dl.rs | Calls NtFreeVirtualMemory + zeroizes on drop |

### Key Detail: `#[must_use]`
```rust
#[must_use]
pub struct SpoofGuard { /*... */ }
```
Forces callers to bind to a variable. Without `#[must_use]`, a caller might write:
```rust
spoof_return_address(); // Guard dropped immediately — no spoofing!
```

## OnceLock Singleton Pattern
Thread-safe lazy initialization without external crates.

```rust
static MAP: OnceLock<HashMap<u32, (u32, usize)>> = OnceLock::new();

fn syscall_map() -> &'static HashMap<u32, (u32, usize)> {
 MAP.get_or_init(|| { /* expensive init */ })
}
```

Used for: syscall map, Kamui SOCKS5 state, cancellation registries, config.

## Cancellation Registry Pattern
Per-module pattern for cancellable long-running operations.

```rust
mod cancel_registry {
 static CANCELLED: OnceLock<Mutex<HashSet<u32>>> = OnceLock::new();

 pub fn cancel(id: u32) { get().lock().unwrap().insert(id); }
 pub fn is_cancelled(id: u32) -> bool { get().lock().unwrap().contains(&id) }
 pub fn clear(id: u32) { get().lock().unwrap().remove(&id); }
}
```

Used by: Byakugan (scan_id), Kotoamatsukami (job_id), Amaterasu (job_id).

## Compiler-Proof Memory Zeroing
```rust
fn secure_zero_memory(buf: &mut [u8]) {
 for byte in buf.iter_mut() {
 unsafe { std::ptr::write_volatile(byte as *mut u8, 0); }
 }
}
```
`write_volatile` prevents the compiler from eliding the zeroing (since the buffer may not be read after clearing).

## mem::replace + mem::forget for Secure Wipe
```rust
fn secure_wipe(s: &mut String) {
 let old = std::mem::replace(s, String::new());
 // old now contains the sensitive data
 unsafe { 
 // zero the backing allocation
 let bytes = old.as_bytes_mut();
 std::ptr::write_bytes(bytes.as_mut_ptr(), 0, bytes.len());
 }
 std::mem::forget(old); // prevent destructor from running on zeroed memory
}
```

## thread_local! for Hook Callbacks
Windows hooks require global state that's accessible from C callbacks. Pattern:
```rust
thread_local! {
 static HOOK_DATA: RefCell<Option<Arc<Mutex<Vec<KeyEntry>>>>> = RefCell::new(None);
}
```
Used by keylogger for WH_KEYBOARD_LL hook callback.

## Conditional Compilation for Cross-Platform
```rust
#[cfg(windows)]
mod win_impl { /* actual implementation */ }

#[cfg(not(windows))]
pub fn some_func() -> Result<()> { Ok(()) } // no-op stub
```
Allows the crate to compile on non-Windows for development/testing.

## Manual FFI with #[link]
Instead of using the `windows` crate for everything:
```rust
#[link(name = "kernel32")]
extern "system" {
 fn ConvertThreadToFiber(lpParameter: *mut c_void) -> *mut c_void;
}
```
Used when only 1-2 functions are needed from a DLL — avoids pulling in large crate dependencies.

## DJB2 Hash for String Resolution
All function names resolved at runtime via DJB2 hash — no string literals in binary:
```rust
fn djb2(s: &[u8]) -> u32 {
 let mut hash: u32 = 5381;
 for &byte in s {
 hash = hash.wrapping_mul(33).wrapping_add(byte as u32);
 }
 hash
}
```

## Macro for Error Cleanup
```rust
macro_rules! bail_close {
 ($handle:expr, $msg:expr) => {{
 NtClose($handle);
 return Err(anyhow!($msg));
 }};
}
```
Used in process_hollow.rs for resource cleanup on error paths.

## Build-Time Configuration Embedding
```rust
// build.rs
fn main() {
 for line in std::fs::read_to_string(".env").unwrap().lines() {
 if let Some((key, val)) = line.split_once('=') {
 println!("cargo:rustc-env=EMBEDDED_{}={}", key, val);
 }
 }
}
```
Enables single-file deployment without a separate config file.

## Selection Lock Pattern
Compile-time configuration via embedded YAML:
```rust
const SELECTION_LOCK_JSON: &str = include_str!(concat!(
 env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"),
 "/../../framework/generated/selection.lock.yaml"
));

static CONFIG: OnceLock<SelectionLock> = OnceLock::new();

pub fn current() -> &'static SelectionLock {
 CONFIG.get_or_init(|| serde_json::from_str(SELECTION_LOCK_JSON).unwrap())
}
```
All runtime behavior determined by a build-time artifact.

